alex: Quick check — I'm about to land a Terraform change to wire the inference service SA to the KMS key. Can someone sanity-check the IRSA <-> KMS bits?

marta: pinging @alex — drop the TF snippet and the trust policy you're planning. quick thumbs up or :shrug:.

alex: here's the minimal changes I'm adding to our shared infra module:

```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role" "inference_irsa_role" {
  name = "rdw-inference-irsa-${var.env}"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Federated = var.oidc_provider_arn }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity"
      Condition = {
        StringEquals = { "${var.oidc_provider_url}:sub" = "system:serviceaccount:${var.ns}:${var.sa_name}" }
      }
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_kms_grant" "inference_key_grant" {
  name = "rdw-inference-grant-${var.env}"
  key_id = var.kms_key_id
  grantee_principal = aws_iam_role.inference_irsa_role.arn
  operations = ["Encrypt", "Decrypt", "GenerateDataKey"]
}
```

alex: Also plan to keep the KMS key policy untouched (organization admins manage it) and rely on grants for service access.

sam: That looks fine. couple of notes: 1) grants are ephemeral in that they can be revoked, but they don't survive key rotation in the same way as key policy principals — but for our use-case (service role) grants are ok. 2) make sure the grantee_principal is the role ARN (not the role ID).

marta: small nit: the trust policy condition uses the full oidc path — in our cluster the issuer URL in TF is "oidc.eks.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/id/ABC123" so the key in StringEquals should be "oidc.eks.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/id/ABC123:sub". otherwise AssumeRole fails.

jorge: also, we need kms:ViaService if the request is coming from lambda or s3, but not for plain STS role usage. Not needed here.

alex: good call on the issuer path — i'll interpolate var.oidc_provider_url exactly. one more question: does anyone object to granting GenerateDataKey so the sidecar can do envelope encryption locally?

sam: that's expected. just confirm the sidecar uses the role's temporary creds. if it's using pod-level env var keys (bad) we'd need different flow.

marta: also add a short note in the module README: "KMS grants created by this module can be revoked by admins; for persistent membership add principals to key policy." saves future head-scratching.

infra-bot: terraform plan for module-refactor showed: + aws_iam_role.inference_irsa_role, + aws_kms_grant.inference_key_grant  (no diffs to key policy)

alex: thanks all — i'll push the PR referencing this thread and include the README note. tagging @marta for review.

marta: will review after lunch. :+1:
